# Line endings are LF in the repository and LF in every working tree.
#
# Without this, Git converts text files to CRLF when checking out on Windows.
# Prettier then reports every file in the repository as incorrectly formatted,
# and the same mismatch reaches ESLint and any test that compares file contents
# byte for byte. It fails on Windows and is invisible on macOS — which is the
# category of bug ADR-0002 makes Windows the primary test platform for.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary files must never be line-ending converted. The fixture PDFs arriving at
# MS-03 are the reason this matters here: a converted PDF is a corrupt PDF, and
# it would corrupt silently.
*.pdf binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.icns binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
